#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""The root half of the Black Ops bar plugin.

This file is installed by bin/black-ops-install as
/usr/local/lib/omarchy-black-ops/apply, owned by root, and a sudoers drop-in
lets one account run it without a password with exactly one of the verbs
below as its only argument. Everything the plugin does that needs root is
here, and nothing else is.

The rules it keeps:

- It accepts one argument, and that argument must be one of VERBS. No verb
  takes a path, a host name or any other text, so the account allowed to run
  it can choose which of these few changes to make and nothing more.
- It refuses to run unless it is root, and unless its own file and every
  folder above it are owned by root and writable by nobody else. A copy that
  someone else could edit is not a copy worth trusting with root.
- It never follows a symbolic link when it writes. Folders are opened one
  component at a time with O_NOFOLLOW, files are written to a new name in the
  same folder and renamed over the old one, and a target that turns out to be
  a link is refused rather than written through.
- It prints one short line saying what it did, and never the contents of a
  file. It keeps no log of its own.

Python is started with -I, so no environment variable and no user site folder
can change which modules it loads. Commands it runs are given by absolute path
with a fixed, minimal environment.
"""
